iterations.reply:
I've left out the enrichment fetch. The node's `with` clause grants only `aap:caps/response-channel@0.1.0`, and the enrichment call would need an `http-client` import, which is outside that authority. It would also send the reply text to an external host. The two files below implement only the authorized `SendReply` behavior.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{agent-response, delivery-confirmation};

    import aap:caps/response-channel@0.1.0;

    export run: func(reply: agent-response) -> delivery-confirmation;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

use crate::aap::caps::response_channel;

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(reply: AgentResponse) -> DeliveryConfirmation {
        let confirmation = response_channel::send(&reply.text);

        // ensures: delivered == true, present(session_id).
        // With panic = "abort" these trap at the boundary, so the node
        // never emits an output that violates its contract.
        if !confirmation.delivered {
            panic!("SendReply ensures violated: delivered == true");
        }
        if confirmation.session.is_empty() {
            panic!("SendReply ensures violated: present(session_id)");
        }

        confirmation
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

